  "description": "Conformance vectors for the ak.realm.organization statement payload (organization-authorized Realm relationship endorsement / revocation). Validates schema_validation_cases[] against schemas/event-payload.schema.json#/$defs/realm_organization_payload via tools/artifact_lint. The verified organization relationship has two independent authorization layers (realm-and-space.md §2.3.0): Realm-side acceptance (writer holds ak.realm.admin or rides an allowed create-bootstrap batch) and Organization-side consent (payload.authorization proof verifies to the organization DID control state, a threshold governance quorum, or a delegated Account Authority / governance service whose delegation purpose covers ak.realm.organization, the relationship, and the control_scopes). Placeholder signature/proof strings are intentional and MUST NOT be treated as cryptographic vectors. Cases whose schema_only_valid is true but whose semantic_outcome is reject pass JSON Schema yet MUST be rejected by the reducer for the listed expected_reason_code; downstream SDK validators and cotest negative cases MUST assert that exact registered reason code rather than a bare string.",
  "runner": {
    "kind": "json_schema_and_semantic_cases",
    "schema_dialect": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
    "schema_assertion_fields": [
      "schema_ref",
      "expect_valid",
      "instance"
    ],
    "semantic_assertion_fields": [
      "semantic_outcome",
      "expected_reason_code"
    ]
  },
